+Before running Node or npm, use the launcher for your shell. It removes inherited
+`OTEL_*`, `GRAFANA_CLOUD_*`, `COMPOSE_FILE`, Node preload/search-path/proxy controls,
+and npm's Node options for the command. Opening a new terminal alone does not clear inherited
+configuration. In particular, a signal-specific endpoint overrides a generic
+OTLP endpoint, and `NODE_OPTIONS` can load instrumentation before a script starts.
+The launchers leave the caller's environment unchanged. They preserve the
+intentional `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`, `DEMO_HTTP_PORT`, and `PIPELINE_APP_URL`
+settings used for an isolated local stack.
+
+PowerShell:
+
+Check `Get-ExecutionPolicy -List` and `Get-ExecutionPolicy` before running a
+`.ps1` launcher. If the effective policy is `Restricted` and your organization
+permits local scripts, open a temporary session from this checkout with
+`powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned`, then continue below.
+`exit` closes that session; no persistent policy changes are needed. A process
+policy cannot override Group Policy. If it remains blocked, follow your
+organization's policy. See [PowerShell execution policies](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_execution_policies).
